Z||000008||Kelvin Vivian||04-16-2001||05:08 PM||||Yup, yup... Fiero 4-cyls with the factory "GT" dual exhaust setup are:<P>1) 84 Indy Fieros ~2000 made<BR>2) 86 SE 4-cyl ~4300 made<BR>3) 87 SE 4-cyl ~1400 made<P>Blue Fieros ~4400 made<P>Vlad, was the car a 5-spd or auto?<p>[This message has been edited by Kelvin Vivian (edited 04-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Vlad||04-16-2001||05:23 PM||||It was blue 87 SE.  5 speed. 105k KM  (60 000 miles)<P>Vancouver local car according to the papers.<BR>I checked it all around. Virtually - no rust. Very clean in and out. <P>The guy who is selling is a dealer and the car has been sitting in the lot for more than a year. Still very good looking car. <BR>Asked price were 3400 canadian. The guy dropped to 3K right away. <BR>I assume the car can be bought for less then 2K US.<P>Nice car.<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Mattsfiero||04-17-2001||08:31 AM||||I agree with replacing the typical 2.5 exhaust with a 2.8 exhaust. I do know of one other car that that was done to. The exauhsts are fitted the same and do mount the same. the only difference is the quad pipes and a little more of a weak rumble.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Matt<BR>85 custom coupe<BR>Mattsfiero@aol.com<BR>www.anglefire.com/ma3/mattsfiero||||reg||1
